    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (69.26) and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (67.68) headline our offensive output, representing the most stable high-floor options. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** benefits from a significant platoon advantage against Scott, while **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** continues to showcase elite contact quality (0.377 xwOBA), providing the necessary ballast for our Roto categories. **Josh Jung** (66.28) is our primary target for power production, as the combination of a favorable hitter\u2019s park and a soft matchup against Quintana allows him to transcend his base projection. While **Gunnar Henderson** holds an elite pedigree, his matchup against a high-tier arm in McClanahan and his current platoon drag result in a more conservative score of 48.95; he remains in the lineup primarily for his multi-category contribution, specifically the potential for opportunistic stolen bases against a pitcher with a slow delivery.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision involved our bench, where **Nolan Schanuel** (49.01) was the final man left out. Despite a respectable score, his lack of high-end speed compared to outfielders like **Josh Lowe** or **Jackson Merrill** caused him to miss the cut in our SB-prioritized framework. Meanwhile, we continue to monitor the status of **Luis Robert Jr.** on the IL, as his absence necessitates a heavy reliance on the consistency of **Kyle Tucker** (65.46) to anchor the outfield. We are keeping a close watch on **Gunnar Henderson**, whose matchup risk is mitigated by the 100% stolen base expectation against the battery, but owners should be wary of the high-strikeout nature of his opponent. With **Jordan Westburg**, **Jorge Polanco**, **Jacob Wilson**, **Heliot Ramos**, **Nasim Nunez**, and **Gage Workman** remaining in reserve, our depth is positioned to pivot should any late-breaking lineup changes occur for **Drake Baldwin**, **Liam Hicks**, **Sam Antonacci**, **Andy Pages**, **Dominic Smith**, **Brady House**, **Miguel Vargas**, or **Coby Mayo**.",
